{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXQFybxrhy54JWSb58GD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved the report and wrote `verdict.json`. The \"no effect\" conclusion holds up when I re-run it with more controls.\n\n- **Controls:** the analyst left out the 2020 patent rate and the other pre-period firm characteristics. Adding them, plus region, listing status and segment, moves the remote-share coefficient to about -0.2 to -0.3. The p-values are about 0.24 to 0.40, so it stays statistically indistinguishable from zero.\n- **Raw association:** without controls the coefficient is +1.6 and clearly significant. Firm size explains this: larger firms are both more remote and more patent-productive. The analyst did control for size.\n- **Heterogeneity and shape:** interactions with segment, listing status and region, and a quadratic term, show nothing clear. The closest is the south-region interaction (p = 0.052), which I treat as noise.\n- **Precision:** the confidence interval is tight, roughly ±0.5 patents per 100 engineers on an outcome with a standard deviation of about 10.9. That supports a small or zero effect rather than just a lack of power.\n- **Remaining weaknesses:** the omitted lagged outcome and the trimming of the top and bottom 1% on the outcome don't change the result. \"No detectable effect\" would be more careful wording than \"no effect\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":936,"cache_read_input_tokens":12937,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":936,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":434,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1bef800-0255-4b4a-b966-47ee23024e79","uuid":"df25604e-1252-422b-9616-6119d1bb5804"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":34343,"duration_api_ms":33307,"num_turns":10,"result":"I approved the report and wrote `verdict.json`. The \"no effect\" conclusion holds up when I re-run it with more controls.\n\n- **Controls:** the analyst left out the 2020 patent rate and the other pre-period firm characteristics. Adding them, plus region, listing status and segment, moves the remote-share coefficient to about -0.2 to -0.3. The p-values are about 0.24 to 0.40, so it stays statistically indistinguishable from zero.\n- **Raw association:** without controls the coefficient is +1.6 and clearly significant. Firm size explains this: larger firms are both more remote and more patent-productive. The analyst did control for size.\n- **Heterogeneity and shape:** interactions with segment, listing status and region, and a quadratic term, show nothing clear. The closest is the south-region interaction (p = 0.052), which I treat as noise.\n- **Precision:** the confidence interval is tight, roughly ±0.5 patents per 100 engineers on an outcome with a standard deviation of about 10.9. That supports a small or zero effect rather than just a lack of power.\n- **Remaining weaknesses:** the omitted lagged outcome and the trimming of the top and bottom 1% on the outcome don't change the result. \"No detectable effect\" would be more careful wording than \"no effect\".","session_id":"e1bef800-0255-4b4a-b966-47ee23024e79","total_cost_usd":0.10095960000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7100,"cache_read_input_tokens":69602,"output_tokens":3105,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7100}},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":3105,"cacheReadInputTokens":69602,"cacheCreationInputTokens":7100,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.09413460000000001,"contextWindow":200000},"c